# Installation

## 1. Clone Repository

bash git clone <repository-url> cd psa 

---

## 2. Create Conda Environment

bash conda env create -f environment.yml 

---

## 3. Activate Environment

bash conda activate psa 

---

## 4. Install PSA Package

bash python -m pip install -e . 

---

# Starting the Application

## Tkinter GUI (legacy)

bash python main.py 

or:

bash python -m psa.GUI 

---

## PySide6 GUI (recommended)

bash python -m psa.GUI_pyside6 

---

## Dash GUI (browser GUI - not recommended)

bash python -m psa.GUI_dash 

Then open the shown localhost address in your browser.

Usually:

text http://127.0.0.1:8050 

---

# Using the Application

## 1. Load a Pulse Sequence

You can:

- Enter a pulse sequence file
- Browse for a file
- Create/edit sequences using the editor

Supported formats:

- .csv
- .bruker
- generated pulse sequences

---

## 2. Adjust Parameters

Main parameters:

| Parameter | Description |
|---|---|
| Pulse Amplitude | Maximum RF amplitude |
| Vector Length | Magnetization vector length |
| Time/Pulse | Pulse duration |
| Offset | Frequency offset |
| Scaling | RF scaling |
| InpoFact | Interpolation factor |
| x_Expand | Visual x-axis expansion |

---

## 3. Refresh / Recalculate

Press:

- Refresh button
- ENTER key

to recompute all plots and analysis.

---

## 4. Interactive Sliders

Use sliders for:

- Amplitude scaling
- Offset variation

Playback buttons automatically sweep parameters to visualize curve evolution dynamically.

---

## 5. Stability Calculations

Open the Stability tab and configure:

- Amplitude range
- Offset range
- Stability mode

Then click:

text Calculate Stability 

---

## 6. Quality Images

Configure:

- Input directory
- Output directory
- Resolution
- Scan range
- Calculation type

Then calculate and export quality images.

---

# Pulse Sequence Syntax

Example:

text R(100, 0, 50); R(100, 90, 50);  PR(100, 0, 360, 90); 

## Commands

### Rectangular Pulse

text R(amplitude [%], phase [°], duration [µs]); 

### Phase Ramp Pulse

text PR(amplitude [%], start phase [°], end phase [°], duration [µs]); 

